}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Thanks be to God, who gives us the victory through our Lord\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Jesus Christ.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 1 Corinthians 15:57}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 If then you have been raised with Christ, seek the things that\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 are above, where Christ is, seated at the right hand of God.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Colossians 3:1}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Christ has entered, not into a sanctuary made with hands, a\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 copy of the true one, but into heaven itself, now to appear in\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 the presence of God on our behalf.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Hebrews 9:24}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 You shall receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 you; and you shall be my witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Judea, and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Acts 1:8}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Trinity Sunday}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Holy, holy, holy is the Lord God Almighty, who was, and is,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and is to come!  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Revelation 4:8}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 All Saints and other Major Saints' Days}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 We give thanks to the Father, who has made us worthy to\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 share in the inheritance of the saints in light.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Colossians 1:12}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 You are no longer strangers and sojourners, but fellow\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 citizens with the saints and members of the household of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 God.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Ephesians 2:19}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Their sound has gone out into all lands, and their message to\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 the ends of the world.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm 19:4}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Occasions of Thanksgiving}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Give thanks to the Lord, and call upon his Name; make\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 known his deeds among the peoples.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm 105:1}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 At any Time}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Jesus Christ.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Philippians 1:2}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 I was glad when they said to me, "Let us go to the house of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 the Lord."  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm 122:1}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 be acceptable in your sight, O Lord, my strength and my\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 redeemer.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm 19:14}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Send out your light and your truth, that they may lead me,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and bring me to your holy hill and to your dwelling.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm 43:3}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 The Lord is in his holy temple; let all the earth keep silence\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 before him.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Habakkuk 2:20}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 The hour is coming, and now is, when the true worshipers\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 will worship the Father in spirit and truth, for such the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Father seeks to worship him.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 John 4:23}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Thus says the high and lofty One who inhabits eternity,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 whose name is Holy, "I dwell in the high and holy place and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 also with the one who has a contrite and humble spirit, to\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 revive the spirit of the humble and to revive the heart of the \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 contrite."  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Isaiah 57:15}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
